{"step_index":1279,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T01:28:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T04:28:44+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T04:28:44+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.system_generated/tasks/task-1277.log`\nTotal Lines: 841\nTotal Bytes: 18482\nShowing lines 1 to 800\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"The public surface: `client.parse.run(...)`, `client.extract.run(...)`.\r\n2: \r\n3: \r\n4: \r\n5: WHY A FACADE AT ALL\r\n6: \r\n7: ───────────────────\r\n8: \r\n9: openapi-generator produces `ParseApi(api_client).parse_run(...)` across four\r\n10: \r\n11: unrelated Api classes. That is not the surface openapi.yaml says we ship — the\r\n12: \r\n13: spec declares `tags` + `x-sdk-method-name` per operation precisely so the call\r\n14: \r\n15: reads `client.parse.run(document)` (decision N1, API v2 Surface Proposal), and\r\n16: \r\n17: no generator reads those. This module is where that declaration becomes real.\r\n18: \r\n19: \r\n20: \r\n21: It also supplies three things the generator cannot:\r\n22: \r\n23: \r\n24: \r\n25: 1. `extract.from_document(...)`. POST /api/v2/extract declares BOTH an\r\n26: \r\n27:    application/json body (ExtractRequest, the parse_id flow) and a\r\n28: \r\n29:    multipart/form-data body (ExtractDocumentRequest, the raw-document flow).\r\n30: \r\n31:    openapi-generator emits only the first and drops the second without a\r\n32: \r\n33:    warning — ExtractDocumentRequest is absent from the generated models\r\n34: \r\n35:    entirely. One of the three launch flows, silently missing, in both Python\r\n36: \r\n37:    and TypeScript. It is reconstructed here over the generated transport.\r\n38: \r\n39: 2. `jobs.stream(...)`. The SSE progress stream the service really serves.\r\n40: \r\n41: 3. `schema=` instead of `var_schema=`. The generator renames the field to dodge\r\n42: \r\n43:    Pydantic's `BaseModel.schema()`; t\n<truncated 18114 bytes>\nob_id)\r\n728: \r\n729: \r\n730: \r\n731:     def stream(\r\n732: \r\n733:         self,\r\n734: \r\n735:         job_id: str,\r\n736: \r\n737:         *,\r\n738: \r\n739:         output: str | None = None,\r\n740: \r\n741:         include: list[str] | None = None,\r\n742: \r\n743:     ) -> Iterator[JobEvent]:\r\n744: \r\n745:         \"\"\"Progress events for a running job, as they happen.\r\n746: \r\n747: \r\n748: \r\n749:         The same resource as `get(job_id)`, selected by Accept — not a second\r\n750: \r\n751:         route. Yields `status` events on every public status change and then\r\n752: \r\n753:         exactly one terminal `result` or `error`, after which the stream ends.\r\n754: \r\n755:         Keep-alive comments are consumed here and never surface as events.\r\n756: \r\n757:         \"\"\"\r\n758: \r\n759:         # The terminal `result` event carries the same representation the\r\n760: \r\n761:         # JSON path would return, so these have to reach the stream too — a\r\n762: \r\n763:         # stream that could only ever deliver the server default would be a\r\n764: \r\n765:         # second-class way to read the same resource.\r\n766: \r\n767:         query: dict[str, Any] = {}\r\n768: \r\n769:         if output is not None:\r\n770: \r\n771:             query[\"output\"] = output\r\n772: \r\n773:         if include:\r\n774: \r\n775:             query[\"include\"] = include\r\n776: \r\n777: \r\n778: \r\n779:         url = f\"{self._client._server_url}/api/v2/jobs/{quote(job_id, safe='')}\"\r\n780: \r\n781:         if query:\r\n782: \r\n783:             url = f\"{url}?{urlencode(query, doseq=True)}\"\r\n784: \r\n785: \r\n786: \r\n787:         return stream_job_events(\r\n788: \r\n789:             url=url,\r\n790: \r\n791:             headers=self._client._request_headers(),\r\n792: \r\n793:             timeout_seconds=self._client._timeout_seconds,\r\n794: \r\n795:             retries=self._client._retries,\r\n796: \r\n797:         )\r\n798: \r\n799: \r\n800: \r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
